<article class="env-corollary" id="05E5">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/05E5">Corollary <span data-tag="05E5">7.6.3.11</span>.</a> Let $n$ be an integer and suppose we are given a pullback diagram </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[ \xymatrix@R =50pt@C=50pt{ X' \ar [r] \ar [d]^{f'} &amp;  X \ar [d]^{f} \\ Y' \ar [r] &amp;  Y } \]
</div>
<p> in the $\infty $-category $\operatorname{\mathcal{S}}$. If $f$ is $n$-truncated, then $f'$ is $n$-truncated. If $f$ is $n$-connective, then $f'$ is $n$-connective. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
<p>
<strong>Proof.</strong>
      Combine Corollaries <a data-tag="03GG" href="/tag/03GG">7.6.3.10</a>, <a data-tag="056B" href="/tag/056B">3.5.9.12</a>, and <a data-tag="051F" href="/tag/051F">3.5.1.25</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
</p>
</article>
